#: templates/admin/documentation.php:530
msgid "How My Site Hand Works Under the Hood"
msgstr ""

#: templates/admin/documentation.php:534
msgid "Instead of forcing you to install complex software on your server, My Site Hand uses your existing WordPress site itself as the connection gateway. Here is exactly what happens when your AI client communicates with your site:"
msgstr ""

#: templates/admin/documentation.php:539
msgid "Secure Web Endpoint (SSE)"
msgstr ""

#: templates/admin/documentation.php:540
msgid "The plugin opens a secure web channel on your site using the standard WordPress REST API. AI clients send messages to this endpoint to discover or run tools."
msgstr ""

#: templates/admin/documentation.php:543
msgid "Local Connector (mcp-remote)"
msgstr ""

#: templates/admin/documentation.php:544
msgid "When you run the setup script, it configures a local utility called mcp-remote on your machine. This lightweight utility serves as a secure bridge, passing commands between your local Claude Desktop app and your remote WordPress site."
msgstr ""

#: templates/admin/documentation.php:547
msgid "Dynamic Mapping & Execution"
msgstr ""

#: templates/admin/documentation.php:548
msgid "When you ask Claude \"List my draft pages\", Claude translates this request into a structured JSON query, passes it to mcp-remote, which forwards it to the plugin. The plugin executes WordPress functions safely (using read-only DB calls), converts the pages to clean text, and sends them back to Claude."
msgstr ""

#: templates/admin/documentation.php:557
msgid "Claude Desktop app (Automated Connection)"
msgstr ""

#: templates/admin/documentation.php:561
msgid "The Dashboard provides a guided two-step command panel. Once you copy your token and save it on the dashboard, you can run the commands to auto-configure Claude Desktop for Windows, macOS, or Linux."
